    },
    " **%@** from your training — %lld km a week at %@ /km over the last eight weeks, after %@." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : " **%1$@** from your training — %2$lld km a week at %3$@ /km over the last eight weeks, after %4$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    " %@ here has no GPS track, so it falls back to Currimus' own rule of thumb — roughly 0.4 s per metre climbed. Rebuild from Health in Settings to replace it." : {

    },
    " Apple keeps its own copy of these zones and does not publish them to other apps, so the two can still differ by a beat or two where the underlying max heart rate differs. If Fitness shows something else, set the max here by hand and the boundaries follow." : {

    },
    " Change anything here by hand and the automatic update stops, until you tap Recalculate." : {

    },
    " None of your trail runs carries a GPS track yet, so these use Currimus' own rule of thumb instead — roughly 0.4 s of the run's time attributed to each metre climbed, and less than half of that given back on the way down. Rebuild from Health in Settings to replace it with the real thing." : {

    },
    " Nothing in the last four months reached that distance, so the first number describes the shape you were in then." : {

    },
    " Same pace, %lld bpm higher than it used to be. Heat, fatigue or a hard block will do that." : {

    },
    " Same pace, %lld bpm lower than it used to be — that is fitness." : {

    },
    " Same pace, same heart rate." : {

    },
    " The second number is an extrapolation — your volume and pace sit outside the range that study covered, so read it as a direction rather than a time." : {

    },
    " These are yours right now — you changed them by hand, so the automatic update leaves them alone until you tap Recalculate." : {

    },
    " Your longest run is still well short of the race, which neither model can see." : {

    },
    " Your speed is ahead of your training: that gap is long runs and weekly volume." : {

    },
    " Your training is ahead of your racing: the endurance is there, the sharpness is not." : {

