    },
    "Without location there is no route, climb or elevation. Heart rate and distance still record." : {

    },
    "Workout not started" : {

    },
    "You held %lld steps a minute at %@ /km. Aiming for about %lld — five per cent quicker — shortens the stride without changing the pace, so the foot lands under you instead of out in front. That is where most of the impact your knees absorb comes from, after %@. It helps to imagine running on a slippery path: short, light, frequent steps." : {
